{
  "headline": "Aztreonam is not on FDA's shortage list; three Corvale sites hold 10 to 20 days of supply and the top alternate source is E.R. Squibb & Sons, L.L.C. from the Bristol-Myers Squibb Company Princeton plant",
  "headline_cites": ["D4", "D1", "D2", "D3", "D5"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's drug shortage list shows aztreonam is not listed as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["D4"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East holds 261 vials of the 1 g injection at 13.2 vials per day, providing 19.8 days on hand.",
      "cites": ["D1"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale General holds 255 vials at 15.4 vials per day, providing 16.5 days on hand.",
      "cites": ["D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale Lakeside holds 42 vials at 4.1 vials per day, providing 10.1 days on hand.",
      "cites": ["D3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule-ranked first alternate manufacturer is E.R. Squibb & Sons, L.L.C., which is not on FDA's shortage list today and uses the Bristol-Myers Squibb Company Princeton plant.",
      "cites": ["D5"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A second alternate is Fresenius Kabi USA, LLC, also not on the shortage list, whose plant last received a VAI classification on 2023-10-13.",
      "cites": ["D6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A third alternate is Hospira, Inc., not on the shortage list, though its label names no plant we could place.",
      "cites": ["D7"]
    }
  ]
}
